     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg of metformin per day**. The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2550 mg/day**, and for extended-release it's **2000 mg/day**. This order is twice the maximum, which raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe stomach side effects even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals.** That's 2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **1000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals.** That's 2000 mg/day, a common maintenance dose.\n\nWhich did you mean? Once you confirm the dose and how often, I'll enter it. If you really do want a dose above the usual maximum, tell me the clinical reason and I can add it as a note on the order. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
